  {
    "id" : "anonymous_argument_in_multiline_closure",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "Comprehensibility",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Anonymous Arguments in Multiline Closures",
    "description" : "Enforces the use of named arguments instead of anonymous arguments (like $0) in multiline Swift closures.",
    "explanation" : "# Anonymous Argument in Multiline Closure\n\nUse named arguments in multiline closures\n\n* **Identifier:** `anonymous_argument_in_multiline_closure`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Rationale\n\nIn multiline closures, for clarity, prefer using named arguments\n\n```swift\nclosure { arg in\n    print(arg)\n}\n```\n\nto anonymous arguments\n\n```swift\nclosure {\n    print(↓$0)\n}\n```\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nclosure { $0 }\n```\n\n```swift\nclosure { print($0) }\n```\n\n```swift\nclosure { arg in\n    print(arg)\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nclosure { arg in\n    nestedClosure { $0 + arg }\n}\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nclosure {\n    print(↓$0)\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
