    "id" : "closure_spacing",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Closure Spacing",
    "description" : "Ensures closure expressions have exactly one space inside each brace.",
    "explanation" : "# Closure Spacing\n\nClosure expressions should have a single space inside each brace\n\n* **Identifier:** `closure_spacing`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** Yes\n* **Kind:** style\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\n[].map ({ $0.description })\n```\n\n```swift\n[].filter { $0.contains(location) }\n```\n\n```swift\nextension UITableViewCell: ReusableView { }\n```\n\n```swift\nextension UITableViewCell: ReusableView {}\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\n[].filter↓{ $0.contains(location) }\n```\n\n```swift\n[].filter(↓{$0.contains(location)})\n```\n\n```swift\n[].map(↓{$0})\n```\n\n```swift\n(↓{each in return result.contains(where: ↓{e in return e}) }).count\n```\n\n```swift\nfilter ↓{ sorted ↓{ $0 < $1}}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
