    "title" : "Avoid Discouraged Object Literals",
    "description" : "This rule discourages the use of object literals like #imageLiteral and #colorLiteral and prefers the use of initializers instead.",
    "explanation" : "# Discouraged Object Literal\n\nPrefer initializers over object literals\n\n* **Identifier:** `discouraged_object_literal`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  image_literal\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  true\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  color_literal\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  true\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet image = UIImage(named: aVariable)\n```\n\n```swift\nlet image = UIImage(named: \"interpolated \\(variable)\")\n```\n\n```swift\nlet color = UIColor(red: value, green: value, blue: value, alpha: 1)\n```\n\n```swift\nlet image = NSImage(named: aVariable)\n```\n\n```swift\nlet image = NSImage(named: \"interpolated \\(variable)\")\n```\n\n```swift\nlet color = NSColor(red: value, green: value, blue: value, alpha: 1)\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet image = ↓#imageLiteral(resourceName: \"image.jpg\")\n```\n\n```swift\nlet color = ↓#colorLiteral(red: 0.9607843161, green: 0.7058823705, blue: 0.200000003, alpha: 1)\n```",
