    "description" : "This rule detects dictionary literals that contain duplicated keys which will cause a runtime crash.",
    "explanation" : "# Duplicated Key in Dictionary Literal\n\nDictionary literals with duplicated keys will crash at runtime\n\n* **Identifier:** `duplicated_key_in_dictionary_literal`\n* **Enabled by default:** Yes\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** lint\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\n[\n    1: \"1\",\n    2: \"2\"\n]\n```\n\n```swift\n[\n    \"1\": 1,\n    \"2\": 2\n]\n```\n\n```swift\n[\n    foo: \"1\",\n    bar: \"2\"\n]\n```\n\n```swift\n[\n    UUID(): \"1\",\n    UUID(): \"2\"\n]\n```\n\n```swift\n[\n    #line: \"1\",\n    #line: \"2\"\n]\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\n[\n    1: \"1\",\n    2: \"2\",\n    ↓1: \"one\"\n]\n```\n\n```swift\n[\n    \"1\": 1,\n    \"2\": 2,\n    ↓\"2\": 2\n]\n```\n\n```swift\n[\n    foo: \"1\",\n    bar: \"2\",\n    baz: \"3\",\n    ↓foo: \"4\",\n    zaz: \"5\"\n]\n```\n\n```swift\n[\n    .one: \"1\",\n    .two: \"2\",\n    .three: \"3\",\n    ↓.one: \"1\",\n    .four: \"4\",\n    .five: \"5\"\n]\n```",
