    "description" : "This rule enforces using the isEmpty property to check if a collection is empty instead of comparing it directly to an empty array or dictionary literal.",
    "explanation" : "# Empty Collection Literal\n\nPrefer checking `isEmpty` over comparing collection to an empty array or dictionary literal\n\n* **Identifier:** `empty_collection_literal`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** performance\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nmyArray = []\n```\n\n```swift\nmyArray.isEmpty\n```\n\n```swift\n!myArray.isEmpty\n```\n\n```swift\nmyDict = [:]\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nmyArray↓ == []\n```\n\n```swift\nmyArray↓ != []\n```\n\n```swift\nmyArray↓ == [ ]\n```\n\n```swift\nmyDict↓ == [:]\n```\n\n```swift\nmyDict↓ != [:]\n```\n\n```swift\nmyDict↓ == [: ]\n```\n\n```swift\nmyDict↓ == [ :]\n```\n\n```swift\nmyDict↓ == [ : ]\n```",
