    "description" : "This rule enforces using the isEmpty property to check for empty strings instead of comparing a string to an empty string literal.",
    "explanation" : "# Empty String\n\nPrefer checking `isEmpty` over comparing `string` to an empty string literal\n\n* **Identifier:** `empty_string`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** performance\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nmyString.isEmpty\n```\n\n```swift\n!myString.isEmpty\n```\n\n```swift\n\"\"\"\nfoo==\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nmyString↓ == \"\"\n```\n\n```swift\nmyString↓ != \"\"\n```\n\n```swift\nmyString↓==\"\"\n```\n\n```swift\nmyString↓ == #\"\"#\n```\n\n```swift\nmyString↓ == ##\"\"##\n```",
