    "id" : "explicit_enum_raw_value",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Explicit Enum Raw Value Assignment",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that enums with raw value types explicitly assign raw values to each case.",
    "explanation" : "# Explicit Enum Raw Value\n\nEnums should be explicitly assigned their raw values\n\n* **Identifier:** `explicit_enum_raw_value`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers {\n  case int(Int)\n  case short(Int16)\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: Int {\n  case one = 1\n  case two = 2\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: Double {\n  case one = 1.1\n  case two = 2.2\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case one = \"one\"\n  case two = \"two\"\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nprotocol Algebra {}\nenum Numbers: Algebra {\n  case one\n}\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: Int {\n  case one = 10, ↓two, three = 30\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: NSInteger {\n  case ↓one\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case ↓one\n  case ↓two\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n   case ↓one, two = \"two\"\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: Decimal {\n  case ↓one, ↓two\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Outer {\n    enum Numbers: Decimal {\n      case ↓one, ↓two\n    }\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
