    "id" : "fallthrough",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Fallthrough in Switch Statements",
    "description" : "This rule enforces avoiding the use of the 'fallthrough' keyword in Swift switch statements.",
    "explanation" : "# Fallthrough\n\nFallthrough should be avoided\n\n* **Identifier:** `fallthrough`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nswitch foo {\ncase .bar, .bar2, .bar3:\n  something()\n}\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nswitch foo {\ncase .bar:\n  ↓fallthrough\ncase .bar2:\n  something()\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
