    "title" : "Enforce FatalError Message",
    "description" : "Ensures that every fatalError call includes a descriptive message.",
    "explanation" : "# Fatal Error Message\n\nA fatalError call should have a message\n\n* **Identifier:** `fatal_error_message`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nfunc foo() {\n  fatalError(\"Foo\")\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nfunc foo() {\n  fatalError(x)\n}\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nfunc foo() {\n  ↓fatalError(\"\")\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nfunc foo() {\n  ↓fatalError()\n}\n```",
