    "description" : "Ensures that file header comments in Swift source files follow a consistent pattern as defined by the project.",
    "explanation" : "# File Header\n\nHeader comments should be consistent with project patterns. The SWIFTLINT_CURRENT_FILENAME placeholder can optionally be used in the required and forbidden patterns. It will be replaced by the real file name.\n\n* **Identifier:** `file_header`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** style\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet foo = \"Copyright\"\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = 2 // Copyright\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = 2\n // Copyright\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\n// ↓Copyright\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// ↓Copyright\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n//  FileHeaderRule.swift\n//  SwiftLint\n//\n//  Created by Marcelo Fabri on 27/11/16.\n//  ↓Copyright © 2016 Realm. All rights reserved.\n//\n```",
