  {
    "id" : "file_name",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Matching File Name to Declared Type or Extension",
    "description" : "Ensures the file name matches a type or extension declared within the file, if any exist.",
    "explanation" : "# File Name\n\nFile name should match a type or extension declared in the file (if any)\n\n* **Identifier:** `file_name`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  excluded\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  [&quot;LinuxMain.swift&quot;, &quot;main.swift&quot;]\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  excluded_paths\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  []\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  prefix_pattern\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  &quot;&quot;\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  suffix_pattern\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  &quot;\\+.*&quot;\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  nested_type_separator\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  &quot;.&quot;\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  require_fully_qualified_names\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  false\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
