  {
    "id" : "implicit_optional_initialization",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce consistent optional initialization",
    "description" : "Ensure optionals are initialized consistently either with = nil or left uninitialized according to configured style (always or never).",
    "explanation" : "# Implicit Optional Initialization\n\nOptionals should be consistently initialized, either with `= nil` or without.\n\n* **Identifier:** `implicit_optional_initialization`\n* **Enabled by default:** Yes\n* **Supports autocorrection:** Yes\n* **Kind:** style\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  style\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  always\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nvar foo: Int? {\n  if bar != nil { }\n  return 0\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nvar foo: Int? = {\n  if bar != nil { }\n  return 0\n}()\n```\n\n```swift\nlazy var test: Int? = nil\n```\n\n```swift\nlet myVar: String? = nil\n```\n\n```swift\nvar myVar: Int? { nil }\n```\n\n```swift\nvar x: Int? = 1\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nprivate var myVar: Int? = nil\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nvar myVar: Optional<Int> = nil\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nvar myVar: Int? { nil }, myOtherVar: Int? = nil\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nvar myVar: String? = nil {\n  didSet { print(\"didSet\") }\n}\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nfunc funcName() {\n    var myVar: String? = nil\n}\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nvar x: Int? = nil // comment\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\npublic var myVar: Int?\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nvar myVar: Optional<Int>\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nvar myVar: Int? { nil }, myOtherVar: Int?\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nvar myVar: String? {\n  didSet { print(\"didSet\") }\n}\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nfunc funcName() {\n  var myVar: String?\n}\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nvar x: Int? // comment\n\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nvar ↓myVar: Int? \n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nvar ↓myVar: Optional<Int> \n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nvar myVar: Int? = nil, ↓myOtherVar: Int? \n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nvar ↓myVar: String? {\n  didSet { print(\"didSet\") }\n}\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: never\n//\n\nfunc funcName() {\n  var ↓myVar: String?\n}\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nvar ↓myVar: Int? = nil\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nvar ↓myVar: Optional<Int> = nil\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nvar myVar: Int?, ↓myOtherVar: Int? = nil\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nvar ↓myVar: String? = nil {\n  didSet { print(\"didSet\") }\n}\n\n```\n\n```swift\n//\n// style: always\n//\n\nfunc funcName() {\n    var ↓myVar: String? = nil\n}\n\n```",
