    "title" : "Avoid Explicit Usage of Default Separator in joined()",
    "description" : "Discourages explicitly specifying the default separator parameter in the joined() method in Swift.",
    "explanation" : "# Joined Default Parameter\n\nDiscouraged explicit usage of the default separator\n\n* **Identifier:** `joined_default_parameter`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** Yes\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet foo = bar.joined()\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = bar.joined(separator: \",\")\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = bar.joined(separator: toto)\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet foo = bar.joined(↓separator: \"\")\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = bar.filter(toto)\n             .joined(↓separator: \"\"),\n```\n\n```swift\nfunc foo() -> String {\n  return [\"1\", \"2\"].joined(↓separator: \"\")\n}\n```",
