  {
    "id" : "no_extension_access_modifier",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Extension Access Modifiers",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that access modifiers (like private, public, internal, fileprivate, open) should not be used on extensions in Swift code.",
    "explanation" : "# No Extension Access Modifier\n\nPrefer not to use extension access modifiers\n\n* **Identifier:** `no_extension_access_modifier`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  error\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nextension String {}\n```\n\n```swift\n\n\n extension String {}\n```\n\n```swift\nnonisolated extension String {}\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\n↓private extension String {}\n```\n\n```swift\n↓public \n extension String {}\n```\n\n```swift\n↓open extension String {}\n```\n\n```swift\n↓internal extension String {}\n```\n\n```swift\n↓fileprivate extension String {}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
