  {
    "id" : "no_grouping_extension",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Grouping Code Using Extensions in the Same Source File",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that extensions should not be used to group code within the same source file.",
    "explanation" : "# No Grouping Extension\n\nExtensions shouldn't be used to group code within the same source file\n\n* **Identifier:** `no_grouping_extension`\n* **Enabled by default:** No\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nprotocol Food {}\nextension Food {}\n```\n\n```swift\nclass Apples {}\nextension Oranges {}\n```\n\n```swift\nclass Box<T> {}\nextension Box where T: Vegetable {}\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nenum Fruit {}\n↓extension Fruit {}\n```\n\n```swift\n↓extension Tea: Error {}\nstruct Tea {}\n```\n\n```swift\nclass Ham { class Spam {}}\n↓extension Ham.Spam {}\n```\n\n```swift\nextension External { struct Gotcha {}}\n↓extension External.Gotcha {}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
