  {
    "id" : "optional_data_string_conversion",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Prefer Failable String Initialization for Data to String Conversion",
    "description" : "This rule enforces using the failable String initializer String(bytes:encoding:) when converting Data to String in Swift.",
    "explanation" : "# Optional Data -> String Conversion\n\nPrefer failable `String(bytes:encoding:)` initializer when converting `Data` to `String`\n\n* **Identifier:** `optional_data_string_conversion`\n* **Enabled by default:** Yes\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** lint\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nString(data: data, encoding: .utf8)\n```\n\n```swift\nString(bytes: data, encoding: .utf8)\n```\n\n```swift\nString(UTF8.self)\n```\n\n```swift\nString(a, b, c, UTF8.self)\n```\n\n```swift\nString(decoding: data, encoding: UTF8.self)\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nString(decoding: data, as: UTF8.self)\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
