    "title" : "Enforce Protocol Property Accessors Order",
    "description" : "Ensures that when declaring properties in Swift protocols, the accessors are ordered as 'get set'.",
    "explanation" : "# Protocol Property Accessors Order\n\nWhen declaring properties in protocols, the order of accessors should be `get set`\n\n* **Identifier:** `protocol_property_accessors_order`\n* **Enabled by default:** Yes\n* **Supports autocorrection:** Yes\n* **Kind:** style\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nprotocol Foo {\n var bar: String { get set }\n }\n```\n\n```swift\nprotocol Foo {\n var bar: String { get }\n }\n```\n\n```swift\nprotocol Foo {\n var bar: String { set }\n }\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nprotocol Foo {\n var bar: String { ↓set get }\n }\n```",
