    "id" : "reduce_boolean",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Performance",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Prefer .allSatisfy() or .contains() over reduce(true/false)",
    "description" : "This rule encourages using `.allSatisfy()` or `.contains()` instead of `reduce(true)` or `reduce(false)` for boolean reductions.",
    "explanation" : "# Reduce Boolean\n\nPrefer using `.allSatisfy()` or `.contains()` over `reduce(true)` or `reduce(false)`.\n\n* **Identifier:** `reduce_boolean`\n* **Enabled by default:** Yes\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** performance\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nnums.reduce(0) { $0.0 + $0.1 }\n```\n\n```swift\nnums.reduce(0.0) { $0.0 + $0.1 }\n```\n\n```swift\nnums.reduce(initial: true) { $0.0 && $0.1 == 3 }\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet allNines = nums.↓reduce(true) { $0.0 && $0.1 == 9 }\n```\n\n```swift\nlet anyNines = nums.↓reduce(false) { $0.0 || $0.1 == 9 }\n```\n\n```swift\nlet allValid = validators.↓reduce(true) { $0 && $1(input) }\n```\n\n```swift\nlet anyValid = validators.↓reduce(false) { $0 || $1(input) }\n```\n\n```swift\nlet allNines = nums.↓reduce(true, { $0.0 && $0.1 == 9 })\n```\n\n```swift\nlet anyNines = nums.↓reduce(false, { $0.0 || $0.1 == 9 })\n```\n\n```swift\nlet allValid = validators.↓reduce(true, { $0 && $1(input) })\n```\n\n```swift\nlet anyValid = validators.↓reduce(false, { $0 || $1(input) })\n```\n\n```swift\nnums.reduce(into: true) { (r: inout Bool, s) in r = r && (s == 3) }\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
