    "title" : "Avoid Redundant String Enum Value",
    "description" : "Enforces omission of explicit string values in Swift enums when the value is identical to the case name.",
    "explanation" : "# Redundant String Enum Value\n\nString enum values can be omitted when they are equal to the enumcase name\n\n* **Identifier:** `redundant_string_enum_value`\n* **Enabled by default:** Yes\n* **Supports autocorrection:** No\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case one\n  case two\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: Int {\n  case one = 1\n  case two = 2\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case one = \"ONE\"\n  case two = \"TWO\"\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case one = \"ONE\"\n  case two = \"two\"\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case one, two\n}\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case one = ↓\"one\"\n  case two = ↓\"two\"\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case one = ↓\"one\", two = ↓\"two\"\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nenum Numbers: String {\n  case one, two = ↓\"two\"\n}\n```",
