  {
    "id" : "trailing_comma",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Trailing Comma in Arrays and Dictionaries",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the avoidance of trailing commas in array and dictionary literals in Swift code.",
    "explanation" : "# Trailing Comma\n\nTrailing commas in arrays and dictionaries should be avoided/enforced.\n\n* **Identifier:** `trailing_comma`\n* **Enabled by default:** Yes\n* **Supports autocorrection:** Yes\n* **Kind:** style\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  mandatory_comma\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  false\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [1, 2, 3]\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = []\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [:]\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [1: 2, 2: 3]\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [Void]()\n```\n\n```swift\nlet example = [ 1,\n 2\n // 3,\n]\n```\n\n```swift\nfoo([1: \"\\(error)\"])\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [Int]()\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [1, 2, 3↓,]\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [1, 2, 3↓, ]\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [1, 2, 3   ↓,]\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [1: 2, 2: 3↓, ]\n```\n\n```swift\nstruct Bar {\n let foo = [1: 2, 2: 3↓, ]\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [1, 2, 3↓,] + [4, 5, 6↓,]\n```\n\n```swift\nlet example = [ 1,\n2↓,\n // 3,\n]\n```\n\n```swift\nlet foo = [\"אבג\", \"αβγ\", \"🇺🇸\"↓,]\n```\n\n```swift\nclass C {\n #if true\n func f() {\n let foo = [1, 2, 3↓,]\n }\n #endif\n}\n```\n\n```swift\nfoo([1: \"\\(error)\"↓,])\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
