    "description" : "This rule enforces that lines in Swift code should not have trailing semicolons.",
    "explanation" : "# Trailing Semicolon\n\nLines should not have trailing semicolons\n\n* **Identifier:** `trailing_semicolon`\n* **Enabled by default:** Yes\n* **Supports autocorrection:** Yes\n* **Kind:** idiomatic\n* **Analyzer rule:** No\n* **Minimum Swift compiler version:** 5.0.0\n* **Default configuration:**\n  <table>\n  <thead>\n  <tr><th>Key</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n  <tr>\n  <td>\n  severity\n  </td>\n  <td>\n  warning\n  </td>\n  </tr>\n  </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n## Non Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet a = 0\n```\n\n```swift\nlet a = 0; let b = 0\n```\n\n## Triggering Examples\n\n```swift\nlet a = 0↓;\n\n```\n\n```swift\nlet a = 0↓;\nlet b = 1\n```\n\n```swift\nlet a = 0↓; // a comment\n\n```",
